  "notes": [
    "Inventory is source-derived for SHA2af12e55ffad68d583db2aea50ad3949fde76035; no endpoints were called by this agent.",
    "No logout/password-reset/delete-account controller route exists in these two modules; do not invent them.",
    "All success responses use {success,message,data} except GET /api/privacy/internal/check-dm returning bare JSON boolean.",
    "User-service error bodies are ErrorResponse {success:false,message,...}; identity errors usually ApiResponse.error wrapping ErrorResponse in data. Missing/invalid bearer returns minimal {success:false,message:'Unauthorized'}.",
    "Internal profile and privacy endpoints are permitAll at owning service security, whereas /api/users/internal/admin/** requires ADMIN. Verify gateway blocks internal access before counting it as secure.",
    "Frontend and service auth currently allow unverified-email account login; OTP verification must not be represented as required bootstrap behavior unless code is changed.",
    "Friend-service profile enrichment swallows Feign errors and may return username:null/displayName:'Kirenz User'; assert values to detect cross-service failure.",
    "The public and internal DM permission endpoints share the User-service policy: either block direction denies contact before receiver privacy or friendship is evaluated.",
    "Registration user-created producer catches Kafka send exceptions and is not transactionally guaranteed. GET privacy/me creates defaults synchronously, so a200 here cannot prove asynchronous user-created delivery; use Kafka/DB fixture observation or downstream birthday scheduling verification.",
    "Refresh endpoint lacks explicit token-type validation; a negative security test using accessToken as refreshToken should flag acceptance rather than treating it as a supported contract.",
    "Fresh run-scoped fixtures prevent duplicate request409 and avoid modifying real friendships/privacy or re-registering a real unverified account. No actual credentials or environment secrets are included."
  ]
}
